{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792347655,"nonce":"Qinu8INR8ZaAqmnVc0N+05gttv8=","title":"Extension Studio: preview an extension's UI and debug its logic while you write it","message":"Goal (user, 2026-10-18): a developer writing a RayScript extension sees its UI beside the code, live, and can debug its logic, in RayDE.\n\nLayout\n- A `.rays` file open as a tab gets a Studio mode: the code editor on the left, the Preview beside it. Saving reloads the extension; the Preview redraws.\n- The bottom panel gets Extension tabs: Console (what the script traced, and its errors with file, line and column; a click opens the line), Elements (the live tree the extension has made, with each element's properties and listeners; selecting one highlights it in the Preview), Activity (a timeline of what crossed the wire: operations, events, remote calls and their answers), State (the signals and computed values with their current values, and which effects read them).\n- Debugging: a gutter breakpoint on a line, Continue / Pause / Step over / Step into / Step out, the call stack, and the variables of the frame; stopping on an error or a `debugger` statement; evaluating an expression in the stopped frame. Breakpoints in an event handler stop it when you click in the Preview.\n- Remote modules the extension imports (rayde.workspace and so on) need an answer while developing: the Studio answers from a mock (a JSON file of canned answers, recorded or edited), and shows each call and its answer in Activity.\n\nBuilt on\n- rayscript-host (crates/rayscript-host in the rayscript repo; rayscript issue 648e334): one extension, one process, JSON lines. The Studio is its first client. RayDE runs it through `sh -c exec ... \u003e log`, writes to its stdin, and reads the log as it grows: the same pattern as Job, since reading a pipe would block the frame loop.\n- The view runtime (rayscript issue 3333c71): operations for the tree, events back.\n- ashui for the Preview. Tags map to ashui elements through a table in RayDE; the utility classes (`flex gap-2 p-4`) are resolved at compile time only in ashui (Tw.setters is `#if macro`), so the first Preview supports a subset RayDE resolves itself. A run-time Tw.apply and a component registry are the asks in 8843dc6 to send to ashui.\n\nWork, in order\n1. ExtensionHost: spawn, send, poll, kill, restart; locate the binary (RAYSCRIPT_HOST, PATH, ../rayscript/target); checks against the real host.\n2. Preview: apply operations to ashui elements; tag table and class subset; events from clicks and typing.\n3. Studio tab: editor and Preview side by side, reload on save, Console with errors that open their lines, Problems for syntax errors as you type.\n4. Elements, Activity and State panels; remote-call mocks.\n5. Debugger: a debugging protocol in rayscript-host and the VM (breakpoints by line, pause at a poll, step, frames and locals, evaluate), then the UI.\n6. Snapshots of the Studio in both themes; README section.\n\nNeeds from others\n- rayscript: debugging support in the VM (names of locals, breakpoints, pause and step at polls, frame inspection); a way to list live signals; the ops/events recording is in the host already.\n- ashui: a code editor gutter with markers (bb19773 asks for extension points), run-time utility classes.","files":null}]}